LOGBOOK.md-25-
LOGBOOK.md:26:- DECISION: One checked-byte ledger owns packet, HEV, SSH, DNS, client relay, rekey, metrics, and reconnect admissions. SSH credit is separate from resident bytes but reserves permitted local storage; failed reads are unknown, never zero or absence.
LOGBOOK.md-27-- REVIEW REWORK: Revision-1 review found that the untracked reserve could be spent, total and incremental reservations were conflated, lane admission had no closed predicate, the reconnect/KEX view appeared to drop a permanent reserve, and the packet-plane target still named the deferred iPhone. Revision 2 makes `B_untracked` a permanent charged row, uses total-capacity rows plus candidate deltas, defines atomic lane admission and exact failed-construction release, separates reconnect from permanent KEX state, and aligns the active target to the named physical Apple-silicon Mac.
LOGBOOK.md:28:- DNS RESIDUAL: The hard candidate ledger is 7,635,554 bytes inside an 8,388,608-byte component budget. Combined with the accepted 9,715,712-byte incremental HEV/bridge peak, it leaves 8,110,080 bytes in the lower 25 MiB engineering envelope. This proves arithmetic fit only; production remains false pending complete physical composition.
LOGBOOK.md-29-- PRESSURE: Deterministic Soft/Pressure/Critical entry, hysteretic one-level recovery, one ordered action table, KEX emergency reservation, atomic replacement reservation, old-transport-first Critical release, and explicit stop replace jetsam-driven or side-queue behavior.
LOGBOOK.md:30:- GAPS: Final watermarks, BDP/window winners, component ceilings, untracked reserve, overlap, and iPhone rows remain evidence-gated. No Apple guarantee, payload capture, flow migration, or weakened gate is asserted.
