LOGBOOK.md-1156-- DECISION: A timed-out global request stays outstanding until its late reply is drained. This deliberately prevents an unnumbered SSH `REQUEST_SUCCESS`/`REQUEST_FAILURE` from being miscorrelated with a newer request; callers can record a miss at `LIBSSH2_ERROR_TIMEOUT` and continue the same operation to restore the request slot.
