LOGBOOK.md:1160:### 1145 — libssh2 adapter remains blocked on server-rekey observability and keepalive replies (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
LOGBOOK.md:1161:- BLOCKER: The accepted `libssh2_session_rekey` fork clears client byte/time/manual trigger initiation only. The exact public header exports no KEX lifecycle callback or generation query. Pinned libssh2 handles inbound `SSH_MSG_KEXINIT` entirely inside private `packet.c`/`transport.c` state, so the adapter cannot truthfully emit `.serverInitiated`, mark `activeKeyExchange`, increment generation, or distinguish server-KEX success/failure through the public boundary.
LOGBOOK.md-1162-- BLOCKER: `libssh2_keepalive_send` writes `keepalive@libssh2.org` with `want_reply=1` but returns after queueing and stores no outstanding request or reply outcome. The public API exposes no generic reply-requiring global request or request-success/failure correlation. Consequently the adapter cannot measure reply RTT, enforce reply timeout/miss allowance, or distinguish acknowledgement from silence.
LOGBOOK.md:1163:- EVIDENCE: The public macOS XCFramework exports only `libssh2_session_rekey`, `libssh2_keepalive_config`, and `libssh2_keepalive_send` among relevant symbols. `keepalive.c:52-96` contains no reply wait/state; inbound server rekey is private at `packet.c:1336-1369` and `transport.c:407-425,1039-1048`. Trace callbacks are unavailable in non-debug builds and are not a supported protocol API.
LOGBOOK.md:1164:- ROUTING: Do not report these gates green or build a mock-only partial adapter. Recommend a separately reviewed minimal fork extension exposing typed server-KEX lifecycle plus a nonblocking reply-correlated global-request/keepalive API; alternatives are explicitly failing the libssh2 candidate or revising the mandatory contract. Exact options and resume decision are attached as `TASK-260715-1ozsb6_server-rekey-keepalive-blocker.md`.
