# TASK-260715-3kimon results

## Implemented policy

Units: KiB = 1024 bytes; bandwidth = integer bits/s; RTT = integer ns. Inputs are capped before multiplication. bulkBytes = clamp(ceil(cappedBandwidth * cappedRTT / 8000000000), bulkMin, bulkMax), using full-width division and saturating sums. relayBytes = min(relayMax, saturatingAdd(relayControl, saturatingMultiply(datagramCount, max(4 + frameBody, 64)))). Initial admission atomically requires channel <= per-channel ceiling, laneReserved + channel <= lane ceiling, globalReserved + channel <= global window ceiling, and committed + window + read + write + metadata <= global ledger ceiling. Adjustment delta = min(cap - outstandingCredit, cap - alreadyReservedWindow, laneHeadroom, globalWindowHeadroom, ledgerHeadroom).

Soft caps new initial windows at the configured 32 KiB candidate. Pressure withholds every adjustment and nonessential ordinary/bulk opens. Critical, rekeying, failed, closing, closed, stale generation, above-low-water, invalid outstanding credit, and insufficient reservation refuse without mutation or a pending side queue. Existing advertised credit is never decremented.

## Deterministic vectors

control=32768; ordinary=65536; bulk at 8000000 bits/s and 64000000 ns=64000; relay at control 32768 plus four 1476-byte framed datagrams=38672. UInt64.max bandwidth/RTT saturates then clamps to 262144. Uncapped measurements produce the same result as their configured capped inputs. Configuration rejects non-32/64 candidates, missing classes, overflowing class capacity, inconsistent ceilings, and protocol windows above UInt32.max.

## Reservation reconciliation

Initial reservation owns window plus fixed read/write/metadata capacity. Adjustment grows the reservation but never beyond the immutable channel cap. openFailure, normalClose, reset, cancellation, laneFailure, and lateCallback all use one idempotent release transition. First release returns exact window and ledger bytes; duplicates return zero. Rekey preserves reservations; releaseLane after failure releases every row exactly once. Metrics expose reservations, adjustment bytes, releases, duplicate releases, released bytes, and typed refusal counts.

## Validation

Focused policy plus selected-adapter: exit 0, 12 tests in 2 suites. Randomized vector: 2000 deterministic transitions with every lane/global/ledger invariant checked. Full swift test: exit 0, 506 tests in 42 suites, 25 pre-existing known ReluxNIOSSH-unavailable issues. swift format lint recursive: exit 0 and empty diagnostics. check-core-boundaries: exit 0. swift build: exit 0. git diff --check: exit 0. Logs: .temp/TASK-260715-3kimon/. Production adapter call sites: LibSSH2Transport.performOpenDirectTCPIP and performOpenExecChannel both route through LibSSH2ChannelWindowAdapter.initialReceiveWindow; engine-owned WINDOW_ADJUST remains explicitly unsupported.
