@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# TASK-260715-3kimon results — rework 02
+
+## Implemented policy
+
+Units are binary bytes (`KiB = 1024 B`), bandwidth is integer bits/s, and RTT is integer nanoseconds. Bulk input is capped before multiplication:
+
+```text
+bulkBytes = clamp(
+  ceil(cappedBandwidthBitsPerSecond * cappedRTTNanoseconds / 8_000_000_000),
+  bulkMinimumWindowBytes,
+  bulkMaximumWindowBytes)
+```
+
+The full-width calculation saturates before the configured maximum is applied. Relay credit is:
+
+```text
+relayBytes = min(
+  relayMaximumWindowBytes,
+  saturatingAdd(
+    relayControlWindowBytes,
+    saturatingMultiply(
+      relayBurstDatagramCount,
+      max(4 + relayMaximumFrameBodyBytes, 64))))
+```
+
+Initial admission atomically requires the candidate to fit the immutable per-channel cap, the per-lane window ceiling, the global window ceiling, and the global ledger ceiling including fixed read/write/metadata capacity.
+
+Repeated adjustment separates reusable reserved capacity from new ledger charge:
+
+```text
+reusable = reservedWindowBytes - outstandingAdvertisedCreditBytes
+newlyReservable = min(
+  channelCap - reservedWindowBytes,
+  laneWindowHeadroom,
+  globalWindowHeadroom,
+  ledgerHeadroom)
+adjustmentBytes = min(
+  channelCap - outstandingAdvertisedCreditBytes,
+  reusable + newlyReservable)
+newlyReservedBytes = max(0, adjustmentBytes - reusable)
+```
+
+Only `newlyReservedBytes` grows lane/global/ledger totals. Already-reserved capacity can replenish the same long-lived channel repeatedly without revoking credit or growing reservations.
+
+## Deterministic vectors and gates
+
+- Control: `32768 B`; ordinary: `65536 B`.
+- Bulk at `8_000_000 bits/s` and `64_000_000 ns`: `64000 B`.
+- Relay at `32768 B` control plus four `1476 B` framed datagrams: `38672 B`.
+- `UInt64.max` bandwidth/RTT saturates then clamps to `262144 B`; uncapped measurements equal their configured capped inputs.
+- Soft caps new initial windows at the configured 32 KiB candidate. Pressure withholds every adjustment and nonessential ordinary/bulk opens. Critical, rekeying, failed, closing, closed, stale generation, above-low-water, invalid outstanding credit, and insufficient reservation refuse without mutation or a pending side queue.
+- Configuration rejects non-32/64 candidates, missing classes, overflowing class capacity, inconsistent ceilings, and protocol windows above `UInt32.max`.
+
+Production adjustment gate: `SSHReceiveWindowBudgetLedger.reserveAdjustment` in `Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHReceiveWindowBudgetPolicy.swift`. Production selected-adapter call sites: `LibSSH2Transport.performOpenDirectTCPIP` and `performOpenExecChannel`, both through `LibSSH2ChannelWindowAdapter.initialReceiveWindow`; engine-owned `WINDOW_ADJUST` remains explicitly unsupported.
+
+## Reservation reconciliation
+
+Initial reservation owns window plus fixed read/write/metadata capacity. Four successive fully-consumed replenishment cycles restore outstanding credit to the immutable cap with `newlyReservedBytes == 0` after the first capacity expansion; lane, global-window, and ledger totals remain byte-identical.
+
+`openFailure`, `normalClose`, `reset`, `cancellation`, `laneFailure`, and `lateCallback` share one idempotent release transition. The first owned release returns exact window and ledger bytes; an absent or duplicate release returns zero without retaining the channel UUID. A deterministic `10_000`-channel test performs unknown callbacks followed by open/release for the same IDs and finishes with zero active reservations and exact metrics, proving that idempotency has no unbounded release-tombstone collection. Rekey preserves reservations; `releaseLane` releases every owned row exactly once.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `swift test --filter 'SSHReceiveWindowBudgetPolicyTests|LibSSH2WindowPolicyAdapterTests'`: exit `0`; 13 tests in 2 suites.
+- `swift test`: exit `0`; 519 tests in 43 suites; 25 pre-existing known ReluxNIOSSH-unavailable issues and no failures.
+- `swift format lint --recursive --strict Sources Tests`: exit `0`; empty diagnostics.
+- `make check-core-boundaries`: exit `0`.
+- `swift build`: exit `0`.
+- `git diff --check`: exit `0`.
+
+Logs: `.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon-focused-tests-02.log`, `.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon-full-tests-02.log`, `.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon-format-02.log`, `.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon-boundaries-02.log`, `.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon-build-02.log`, and `.temp/TASK-260715-3kimon-diff-check-02.log`.
