 - ADAPTER: Both libssh2 `libssh2_channel_open_ex` call sites use one tested initial-window conversion. The adapter still truthfully reports consumer-driven adjustment as unsupported; no protocol message is sent outside that adapter.
-- VERIFICATION: Eleven policy tests cover tables, 32/64 KiB, capped and overflowing BDP, relay bursts, all budget ceilings, pressure/lane/generation gates, exact lifecycle reconciliation, and 2,000 deterministic randomized transitions. One selected-adapter test covers all four classes. The full 506-test Swift suite passed with the existing 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues; recursive Swift format, core boundaries, diff check, and `swift build` exited 0.
+- REVIEW REWORK: Revision-1 review found that `reserveAdjustment` treated reserved capacity as one-shot credit and retained an unbounded UUID tombstone set. Adjustment now separates reusable capacity from `newlyReservedBytes`, repeatedly restores outstanding credit to the immutable cap without growing lane/global/ledger totals, rejects impossible outstanding-credit reports, and makes absent release an idempotent zero-release without retaining channel identity.
+- VERIFICATION: Twelve policy tests cover tables, 32/64 KiB, capped and overflowing BDP, relay bursts, all budget ceilings, pressure/lane/generation gates, exact lifecycle reconciliation, four repeated replenishments, 10,000 unknown/released-channel churn cycles, and 2,000 deterministic randomized transitions. One selected-adapter test covers all four classes. The full 519-test Swift suite passed with the existing 25 known unavailable-ReluxNIOSSH issues; strict recursive Swift format, core boundaries, diff check, and `swift build` exited 0.
 
